  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-g-b">Se þe oferhogie þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he heom hlyste, hæbbe him gemæne þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wið God sylfne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" n="20" corresp="#wit-g-b">Se þe oferhogie þæt he heom hlyste, hæbbe him gemaene þæt wið God sylfne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b">Anyone who rejects what he hears from them must settle his dispute with God himself.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wer verschmäht, auf sie zu hören, habe das zu verantworten bei Gott selbst.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever scorns to listen to them, let him answer for it to God himself.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Cn 26.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
